      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:144:4",
      "text": [
        " لَا يُجْلَسُ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَ الْمَرْوَةِ إِلَّا مِنْ جَهْدٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad, from Moalla Bin Muhammad, from one of our companions, from Aban, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abdul Rahman, from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘One cannot sit between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa except from tiredness’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad has narrated from Mu‘alla’ ibn Muhammad, from certain persons of our people, from Aban, from ‘Abd al- Rahman who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘You must not sit down between al-Safa’ and al-Marwah unless you are very exhausted.’” "
        ]
      }
